      "writtenOn": "2025-05-05T20:36:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is a strong start, there\u0027s primarily just a complication around future plans for drawing meshes and vertices provided by users that I don\u0027t want to prevent down the line, but this then impacts the changes in DrawWriter and GlobalCache. I also wrote up some thoughts on the DrawCommands API that we can talk about tomorrow.",
      "revId": "9eee8eb07d9795ceca7250ac0f442cc33b07b2e0",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "46f5dc20_f4208d9e",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/DrawCommands.h",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 184,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-05-05T20:36:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Originally I was going to suggest we use an API like `bindUniformBuffer` that takes a slot enum so there\u0027d only be one `bindDrawBuffer(BindBufferInfo, slot)` function that picked between static, append, indices, or indirect buffers (which I always forget about). Then I refreshed how the CommandBuffers implement things and the only real redundant logic is between static and append buffers, at which point the CB could just share a function and pass in a specific binding index based on the `DrawCommands` switch case its in.  So then I went back to thinking this was solid, but then I started looking at how `bind` could be reused inside `DrawWriter::flushInternal` and it would be pretty simple if it could just add a command that bound to a specific slot enum value.\n\nBut that would require CB\u0027s to specifically handle the index and indirect buffers separately from the static/append data.\n\nAnd there is also some plans to consolidate the uniform structs between render steps and paint params into a single struct and single binding that would need to be updated. This would then remove the slot parameter from bindUniformBuffer entirely, so trying to have bindDrawBuffer match it isn\u0027t so important if it\u0027s going to be simplified.\n\n(although perhaps we just go all the way and have a `bindBuffer(BBI, Slot)` command that covers static, append, index, indirect, and the uniform data slots)?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 170,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 184,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "9eee8eb07d9795ceca7250ac0f442cc33b07b2e0",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
