      "writtenOn": "2025-05-05T20:36:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "One challenge with the current approach is that these APIs don\u0027t allow vertex or index data to come from something other than the main static buffers.\n\nThe one case where this might occur in the future is with the drawVertices and drawMesh APIs. There is a good chance that we will want to create cached Buffers for an SkMesh|SkVertices\u0027s vertices and indices and either use these direct render APIs or use appended instance data to apply per-draw-call parameters w/o having to augment the vertex-rate attribute definition (e.g. we\u0027ll need some way to provide the local-to-device matrix and the ssbo index and paint depth).\n\nWhile the static bindings would be changing in these circumstances, that functionality isn\u0027t inconsistent with the static+append model. It just requires binding be a little more flexible.\n\nI like that the current update guarantees we do the static binds right away, and that it reduces state to just the pending base values. But if we go back to the old model (but with renames like `fBoundStaticData` and `fBoundAppendData`) we should be future proof for the mesh improvements. In that world, GlobalCache could just go back to its original API.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 195,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 208,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "9eee8eb07d9795ceca7250ac0f442cc33b07b2e0",
