      "writtenOn": "2025-05-05T20:36:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Some thoughts on API design (although given my DrawWriter comments, we might end up not needing these changes):\n\n`addStaticResource` is generally available, although currently I think only the static buffers are what is used.  At some point we might want to add dither texture tables or other LUT to the static resources.  So I wouldn\u0027t want to replace `addStaticResource` with these functions, instead their impls might be something like:\n```\nfStaticVertexData \u003d {buffer.get(), 0, buffer-\u003esize()};\nthis-\u003eaddStaticResource(std::move(buffer));\n```\n\nAs-is this API is a bit misleading because adding a static[Vertex|Index]Resource really should only happen once or it erases the BindBufferInfo that was previously added. Having it take a BindBufferInfo is also perhaps too flexible since it\u0027s only ever called (and implicitly expected I think) to be the entire Buffer. In theory if we kept a `setStaticVertexBuffer()` function, it would just need to take an `sk_sp\u003cBuffer\u003e` and could create the BindBufferInfo itself.",
      "range": {
